From 475d167068931bbe88da5398e347aef1b3d5903e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:04:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] perf(steam): start-up times, and less repeated work on
 every Steam start

Times: from events.jsonl and the session script's steps the app now
records, per start, Linux (Play -> the session script running), FEX and
x86-64 client checks, Steam (client start -> first frame) and the total,
first starts (downloads, installs) apart; the launcher's cold start; and
per game launch -> first image (gamescope focuses the game window) ->
smooth (3 s at 20+ fps). Kept in files/startup-times.jsonl and written
to timings.txt in each session's log folder. droiddeck-game-env marks
each launch in the session's launch folder.

Less work per start on an ARMv8.0 CPU:
- x64_prepare rebuilt Valve's runtime library links, an x86 ldconfig
  under FEX and the pruning against the rootfs on every start, one
  basename process per file. They are now rebuilt only when the runtime
  or the rootfs changes (a stamp), with one ln and one rm per directory:
  in a container, 800 links took 5.9 s, now 143 ms, and 9 ms when
  nothing changed.
- droiddeck-steamrt-shim uses ${e##*/} instead of a basename per entry.
- An installed, current ARMv8.0 Proton is checked in the shell, without
  starting Python.
- A client build that reached the screen before starts with
  -noverifyfiles; after an update, a repair or a start that showed
  nothing it verifies as usual (BL_X64_VERIFY_FILES=1 forces it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
